---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import TrustBlock from "../../components/TrustBlock.astro";
import { editorialTeam, carTrustPoints } from "../../data/editorial";

const title = "VW Tiguan II facelift what to check before buying";
const description = "What to inspect on a VW Tiguan II facelift before buying, which weak points deserve the closest look, and what should not scare you too fast.";
const intro = "A facelift Tiguan can still be a sensible buy, but only if you inspect it in the right order. The useful checks are not dramatic: brake behavior, coolant history, warning-light story, battery reserve, tire condition, and whether normal front-end wear has been turned into vague suspension language. Keep the viewing disciplined and make the price follow the condition.";
const modifiedTime = new Date("2026-04-11");
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Guides", href: "/guides/vw-tiguan-ii-facelift-what-to-check-before-buying/" },
  { label: title }
];

const relatedProblems = [
  { href: "/problems/car-shakes-when-braking/", title: "Car shakes when braking", description: "Open this if the test drive hints at front brake vibration.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" },
  { href: "/problems/coolant-level-drops-with-no-visible-leak/", title: "Coolant level drops with no visible leak", description: "Useful when the coolant story feels incomplete or too casual.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" },
  { href: "/problems/epc-light-comes-on-under-acceleration/", title: "EPC light comes on under acceleration", description: "The right next read if the seller story around drivability feels vague.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" }
];

const relatedBest = [
  { href: "/best/best-brake-pads-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best brake pads for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Best if the brakes feel tired but the car still looks worth buying.", eyebrow: "Brake Pads" },
  { href: "/best/best-coolant-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best coolant for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Worth opening if the cooling system history needs a clean reset.", eyebrow: "Coolant" }
];

const relatedComparisons = [
  { href: "/comparisons/vw-tiguan-pre-facelift-vs-facelift/", title: "VW Tiguan pre-facelift vs facelift", description: "Best when you need to separate facelift-specific buying advice from the earlier Mk2 years.", eyebrow: "Generation guide" }
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  intro={intro}
  image="/images/photos/cars/vw-tiguan-2020.webp"
  modifiedTime={modifiedTime}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  editorialSummary="A buyer-focused checklist for the facelift Tiguan, concentrating on the weak points and viewing checks that matter most."
  editorialByline={`By ${editorialTeam.name}`}
  editorialReviewedLabel={`Reviewed ${modifiedTime.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" })}`}
  editorialBadges={["Buying guide", "Generation-specific", "Inspection-focused"]}
>
  <TrustBlock
    title="Best starting point"
    summary="Start here before a viewing or test drive. The goal is to sort the normal weak points from the red flags that should change the price or make you walk."
    byline={`By ${editorialTeam.name}`}
    checkedLabel={`Checked ${modifiedTime.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" })}`}
    points={carTrustPoints}
  />

  <Section title="The short version" intro="If you only need the fast read, these are the checks that matter most.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Test the front brakes properly. Vibration, uneven feel, or rushed recent brake work can turn a tidy SUV into a repeat-spend story fast.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Check coolant level, service history, and whether the seller talks about topping up like it is normal.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Watch for hesitation, EPC history, weak battery behavior, and front-end noises that are being explained away too casually.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What to inspect first" intro="These are the checks worth doing before the walk-around turns into generic used-car small talk.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Brake feel on the test drive, especially from speed and on repeated stops.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Coolant level and whether the engine bay shows signs of small seepage or recent cleanup.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Cold start and battery behavior on a car that has not just been freshly charged for sale day.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Front-end noises over broken pavement, slow turns, and parking-lot maneuvering.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Tire condition and whether the set matches cleanly, especially on 4MOTION cars.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What should lower confidence quickly" intro="These are the things that should change the price conversation or make you move on.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">A seller who normalizes coolant top-ups without a clear repair history.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Brake vibration plus vague talk about recent pads only, with no real rotor or hardware story.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Warning-light history that is described as “just electronics” with no codes or paperwork behind it.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Mixed tires or obvious wear-pattern mismatch on a drivetrain-sensitive setup.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What should not scare you too fast" intro="These are issues that deserve attention, but not instant panic if the rest of the car is strong.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Minor front-end noises that still sound like ordinary wear-item territory.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">A battery nearing replacement age on a short-trip family car.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">A brake refresh that needs to be finished properly rather than the cheapest possible way.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="How to turn the inspection into a decision" intro="The checks are useful only if they change the price, the next step, or the decision to walk away.">
    <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      A good viewing should leave you with one or two specific follow-ups, not a long list of vague seller explanations. If the Tiguan passes coolant, braking, tire, battery, and drivability checks, the buying decision can move to price and trim. If two or more of those checks are uncertain, ask for records, scan results, or a professional inspection before making an offer. The wrong move is treating unresolved warning signs like normal used-car negotiation noise.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="What to do next" intro="Use the failed check to choose the right follow-up page.">
    <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      Coolant concerns should lead to the coolant-loss guide, brake vibration should lead to the braking guide, and EPC or hesitation history should lead to the drivability guide. That keeps the buying process simple: one failed check, one focused follow-up, one price decision. If the viewing produces several failed checks, the simpler answer is usually to keep shopping.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <RelatedLinks title="Related problem guides" intro="Open these if the viewing or test drive already points at a repeat complaint." items={relatedProblems} />
  <RelatedLinks title="Related best-parts guides" intro="Use these when the car is still worth buying but the weak point needs a realistic repair plan." items={relatedBest} />
  <RelatedLinks title="Related comparison guides" intro="Use these when the buying advice changes with phase or drivetrain." items={relatedComparisons} />
</ContentLayout>
